.git
# Same trap as `.env*` below: a bare `.next` matches only the context ROOT, so a
# developer's `apps/web/.next` — build output AND a webpack cache keyed to host
# paths — was riding into the image and poisoning the build inside it.
.next
**/.next
dist
*.log
# `.env*` alone matches only the context ROOT, so `apps/api/.env` was being
# copied into the image — a developer's local secrets baked into a layer.
.env*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
.obsidian
.claude
/tmp
target
**/target
